#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151941 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "150649f4-8b1e-563a-a774-1857d8781212" :question/math-academy-id "e-6247" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151942 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "3923e1d8-73e5-501c-96b5-d6b729260d3a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6249" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) =10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,3].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152042 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/id #uuid "b3b3c2bc-029c-5128-8ea9-00591c6936d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9496" :question/problem "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1 \\leq i \\leq m$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ede9bce-ae38-577e-bacc-87f020612226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257197} {:answer/id #uuid "6500c138-a000-5c85-b486-9284962f6b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257668} {:answer/id #uuid "a76fe671-7d45-5709-aab4-68d346881651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258243} {:answer/id #uuid "afb8a0b8-c91b-53d8-92d2-f3dd9be2ef32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258312} {:answer/id #uuid "f02ab099-1461-5c8c-8a64-5841486261ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afb8a0b8-c91b-53d8-92d2-f3dd9be2ef32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258312} :answer-field/id #uuid "f121ff54-6918-5739-ba1a-2bd0e425da2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e6e7588-d998-5d13-bde2-9f1ecbe236a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123513" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f75718e-b688-57f7-8da7-5b80fb085343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544190} {:answer/id #uuid "6468a315-f6fe-50ef-8ab8-9b9fb69c22ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544305} {:answer/id #uuid "a63af55b-729d-5110-9d15-e2d5527d8efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544445} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2fd54f-96ed-529e-86cd-ae8c068183d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544453} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5808ed-e840-541e-a0a8-45d1856fb2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i-1}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6468a315-f6fe-50ef-8ab8-9b9fb69c22ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544305} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e3b32ab-28f5-5977-974b-8d287db52031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c350d5bc-4404-57ee-b54b-285bbf9a8f0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123516" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=y-2x+10.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-2x+10$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-2x+10$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c4/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})={y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475cfc3a-6171-510d-b62d-087df74508ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544244} {:answer/id #uuid "60822d5f-d7ea-5e7a-bddf-b9af1396fca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544297} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc118c3-8d11-514d-b55e-7e19aba8f614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544427} {:answer/id #uuid "b0dd0081-c931-5fa4-8e54-612dbedeec15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544460} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c13196-907f-5c49-b279-b3931cc9b82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60822d5f-d7ea-5e7a-bddf-b9af1396fca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544297} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe767b7b-e724-5de1-8c65-84a86b708adc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "086ea7e4-b45d-5b48-92bf-b7fd8532a3af" :question/math-academy-id "q-164125" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=16-2x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=16-2x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=16-2x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(16-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9e90ae4-757a-5509-8c52-414b86a9eadb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1}^{2} + 5y_{j - 1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150810} {:answer/id #uuid "be5714ea-bf97-5e96-9523-090827a39d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i}^{2} + 5y_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150811} {:answer/id #uuid "d6372430-2fed-57e7-900f-6682cfd12705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100 - x_{i}^{2} - y_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150812} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2cd2ce-7119-53f9-bca8-cbb8e7db493b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100 - x_{i - 1}^{2} - y_{j - 1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150813} {:answer/id #uuid "65045799-b3da-50d7-99e6-e7cc7532e425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100 - x_{i + 1}^{2} - y_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150814}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a63d29ee-1939-56e6-932a-ce6d23d04a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150809}] :question/id #uuid "579f4499-afd3-5e1e-813e-db4e394ec885" :question/math-academy-id "q-75063" :question/problem "Let $R = [1, 5] \\cdot [2, 7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 100 - x^{2} - y^{2}$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8af1c40d-0b3a-56ea-b1ad-867fdf66005f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x_{i - 1} - y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150816} {:answer/id #uuid "b457fc5b-db07-5313-818b-a0d74a3f6b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} + y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150817} {:answer/id #uuid "03245572-7c39-5c93-bc67-d47eeeb7a37a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - x_{i - 1} - y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150818} {:answer/id #uuid "377d329d-f580-54c6-8ae4-1152badbf469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - x_{i} - y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150819} {:answer/id #uuid "4001ec22-7b30-5ebc-80d6-82d7559de749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x_{i} - y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150820}] :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0cc34b-e069-5efc-9a7e-61cc6ed50f8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150815}] :question/id #uuid "1cb469e6-7b74-5371-89e3-14f53be7cb3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75092" :question/problem "Let $R = [- 1, 1] \\cdot [- 1, 1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 8 - x - y$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02467f85-cb8c-52e6-8524-d58170a0e13a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544090} {:answer/id #uuid "02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544091} {:answer/id #uuid "a11f70f3-8e83-52f0-ae17-f28615c58f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544436} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3f732b-b276-53da-8c54-4876b853e7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544494} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c74500-e7ac-5eaa-beb4-4e1c203d88bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544091} :answer-field/id #uuid "e449d4e6-5069-5c0a-ac4d-1bc5e9e548d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50a1adba-14a0-5a88-abaf-07e0387210e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75306" :question/problem "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [-5,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45327c1c-8d20-5959-acce-f569c289c1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544238} {:answer/id #uuid "5171e819-ae3b-5116-9ea0-748dd049427a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+5{y}_{j}^{2}+5{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544265} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a204c9-fc6a-55fa-a461-0281920bcca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544499} {:answer/id #uuid "db26df39-2212-562e-b5fd-592104bb0910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544560} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b31cd6-f6af-568c-89c7-ecabd44b45b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db26df39-2212-562e-b5fd-592104bb0910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544560} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f8ba87-584e-5b9c-b10e-58f5d8d221b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d148965-74db-5cec-9065-74d36d2d9d5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75307" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,2],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,5].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81211187-e429-5762-8da7-4e1bdfa17158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i} - 9y_{j} + 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150828} {:answer/id #uuid "d8033161-d57f-51a1-83de-16e5172fc800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i} - 9y_{j - 1} + 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150829} {:answer/id #uuid "e739ee5c-7ea0-5272-8ba6-4cc713f400aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i - 1} - 9y_{j - 1} + 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150830} {:answer/id #uuid "f340e40a-0a65-51d5-8dd2-378e02af5d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} - y_{j - 1} + 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150831} {:answer/id #uuid "7c49e799-61a5-5104-bb2d-d888e99d4689" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i - 1} - 9y_{j} + 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150832}] :answer-field/id #uuid "69a5f29a-cfcb-5825-a49b-f6b7a3f7a079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150827}] :question/id #uuid "3919f4a6-1144-5c7c-8ecf-d772c823e93b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75349" :question/problem "Let $R = [0, 1] \\cdot [0, 1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 2x - 9y + 11$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544799 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "138fc8d0-58bb-56a7-a4a1-0ead87eb84d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{y}_{j-1}+2{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544131} {:answer/id #uuid "4db0561e-8dcb-5a82-880f-8f39f966349f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544255} {:answer/id #uuid "64ba2f62-940f-51e4-b382-4ba2a213b726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544306} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a917a8-a750-512e-a24a-d5d184503876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{y}_{j-1}+2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544502} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e8e717-81c6-5340-893f-4ae7e4c8fe45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11{y}_{j}-6{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4db0561e-8dcb-5a82-880f-8f39f966349f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544255} :answer-field/id #uuid "730a83f8-2630-58ea-b90c-e36feb412b1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "27a8dfe2-6a96-5884-8d1c-c8b7f914c19a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75352" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [2,9]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=11y-6x.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=11y-6x$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11y-6x$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c4/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i}.$"}]}
